{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776366238,"nonce":"2TzSz9XGzRtmExq4xF9HmMaZJxg=","title":"Add transient error retry with backoff to HeadlessAgentBase","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen API returns transient errors (500, 502, 503, 504, 429), the agent fails without retry.\n\n## Implementation\n\nAdd retry logic to `HeadlessAgentBase.stream_events()` in `adapters/agents/base.py`:\n\n1. Add constants at module level:\n```python\nTRANSIENT_RETRY_DELAYS = [30, 60, 120]\nTRANSIENT_ERROR_PATTERNS = (\"500\", \"502\", \"503\", \"504\", \"429\", \"rate limit\", \"overloaded\", \"service unavailable\")\n```\n\n2. Add `_is_transient_error(cls, text)` classmethod (like `_is_auth_failure`)\n\n3. Add `_transient_retry_count` instance variable in `__init__`\n\n4. In `stream_events()`, after parsing each event:\n   - If event is AUTH_FAILURE and `_is_transient_error(event.content)`:\n     - Increment retry count\n     - If count \u003c= 3: log warning, sleep(delay), call `self._restart()`, continue\n     - If count \u003e 3: reset counter, yield the AUTH_FAILURE event\n\n5. Add `_restart()` method that stores prompt/workspace from `start()` and can restart the process\n\n6. Remove \"rate limit\" and \"429\" from AUTH_FAILURE_PATTERNS in claude_code.py and openhands.py (add comment that they're handled as transient)\n\n## Tests\nCreate `tests/test_transient_retry.py` with:\n- test_is_transient_error_detects_500\n- test_is_transient_error_detects_429\n- test_retry_count_resets_after_max\n\nKeep tests simple - just test the helper methods, not the full stream_events flow.\n\nREQ: REQ-031","files":null}]}